required_documents:
FOR APPLICANTS WITH A FOREIGN QUALIFICATION — documents to upload to the Elix-Forms pre-evaluation profile (identical list in the EU and non-EU 2026/2027 Additional Notices, second-cycle section):
a) foreign final or provisional university qualification (bachelor);
b) list of completed exams / transcript of records / diploma supplement of the foreign final or provisional bachelor's degree;
c) descriptions of single subjects / syllabus of the foreign bachelor's degree;
d) valid passport;
e) updated curriculum vitae;
f) CIMEA Statements or Declaration of Value of the foreign bachelor's degree*;
g) required language certificate (English B2 or equivalent, issued within the last 5 years)*.
* Items (f) and (g) "may also be submitted after the online pre-evaluation procedure, but [are] required for the final enrolment procedure at the University of Udine."
Plus: payment of a non-refundable €20.00 pre-evaluation fee via PagoPA (bank transfer accepted in specific cases) — "only complete applications will be evaluated, meaning the applications for which the required fee has been duly paid." No motivation letter is required for the master's pre-evaluation (the CV + motivation letter combination is prescribed for the English-taught BACHELOR, Management and Business Analytics, not for the second-cycle courses).

ADDITIONALLY, FOR NON-EU-RESIDENT VISA APPLICANTS — documents to attach to the Universitaly pre-enrolment by 30 June 2026: valid passport; passport-sized photograph; first-cycle university degree (or final/provisional single-cycle master's degree); certificate of English language proficiency at B2 level or equivalent.

FOR HOLDERS OF AN ITALIAN BACHELOR'S DEGREE — no Elix-Forms application; at online immatricolazione, graduates of other Italian universities must self-certify their qualifications indicating exams passed, marks obtained and the SSD of each course, so that the curricular requirements (L-33/L-18 class or the 30 + 18 ECTS SSD thresholds) can be verified, plus proof of English at B2 and, if the final bachelor mark is below 90/110, submission to the Course Council commission's verification of personal preparation. Payment of the first fee instalment via PagoPA completes the enrolment application.
